  "question": {
    "text": "The number of molecules/ion/s having trigonal bipyramidal shape is …….. .</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>PtCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CO</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>5</mn></msub></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> involves sp<sup>3</sup>d hybridisation and hence has trigonal bipyramidal structure.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fe2151f3-3150-427c-8aad-c0804605a7a3.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 303px;\"/></p><p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>  the central atom is surrounded by five bond pairs and no lone paris.<br/>Hybridisation of central atom in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> molecule is sp<sup>3</sup>d giving trigonal bipyramidal shape.</p><h4>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>CO</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>, oxidation state of CO is zero.</h4><p>It has hybridisation =dsp<sup>3</sup>.</p><p>So it has trigonal bipyramidal geometry.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BrF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>;</mo></math> square pyramidal</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>PtCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo></math> square planar</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>;</mo></math> Trigonal planar.</p><p>Hence the answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
